{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl8\pnlcltr\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl9\pnlcrm\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}\pard\plain \s1\sb120\sa60\keepn \b\f5\fs44\lang1044 {\lang2057 
The Norwegian Computer Society
\par }\pard\plain \s21\sb120\sa120 \shading10000 \b\f4\fs28\lang1044 {\lang2057 One of Europe\rquote s oldest computer societies
\par }\pard\plain \fi709 \f4\fs20\lang1044 {\lang2057 The Norwegian Computer Society (NCS) is Norway\rquote s national society of IT-professionals and users, encompassing the IT-industry, corporations in general and research and development ins
titutions. The NCS is an independent and wholly self-financed society. The society turned 40 years in 1993, and is thus one of Europe\rquote 
s oldest computer societies. The NCS today has more than 10400 registered persons as members, and more than 1150 company members.
\par }\pard {\lang2057 
\par }\pard\plain \s21\sb120\sa120 \shading10000 \b\f4\fs28\lang1044 {\lang2057 Advancement of optimal IT usage
\par }\pard\plain \fi709 \f4\fs20\lang1044 {\lang2057 
The major goal of the society is to increase awareness of the possibilities of information technology, and to contribute to advancement and optimal usage of the technology for businesses and the society alike. This 
is done through membership meetings, seminars, conferences and exhibitions, publications and activities towards governmental, political and public institutions and authorities. To a very large degree, the activities within the society are driven by member
s on a voluntary basis. 
\par }\pard {\lang2057 
\par }\pard\plain \s21\sb120\sa120 \shading10000 \b\f4\fs28\lang1044 {\lang2057 Countrywide representation
\par }\pard\plain \fi709 \f4\fs20\lang1044 {\lang2057 The NCS has a countrywide representation, with nine local societies representing Norway\rquote s districts from north to south. The society\rquote 
s strategy and activities are co-ordinated by the main board, which is headed by the society\rquote 
s president and in which each local society is represented by their chairmen. The NCS owns Servicekontoret AS, a limited company which co-ordinates day-to-day operation and the administrative services.  Fourteen people are employed i
n Servicekontoret AS, which is managed by the CEO.
\par }\pard {\lang2057 
\par }\pard\plain \s21\sb120\sa120 \shading10000 \b\f4\fs28\lang1044 {\lang2057 International affiliations
\par }\pard\plain \fi709 \f4\fs20\lang1044 {\lang2057 The NCS is a member of the Nordic Data Union, the Council of European Professional Informatics Societies (CEPIS), and the International Federation of Information Processing (IFIP
). Norway currently has the chair in IFIP, and the vice-presidency in CEPIS. The NCS attaches great importance to international work, which is a prioritised strategic area.
\par }\pard \tx2410 {\lang2057 
\par }\pard\plain \s21\sb120\sa120 \shading10000 \b\f4\fs28\lang1044 {\lang2057 Major NCS goals for 1995
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}}\pard\plain \fi-283\li283{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\f4\fs20\lang1044 {\lang2057 
Increase the activity of our working groups (special interest groups) and to renew the general activities of the Society. The goal is to have a total of 40 working groups by 1996.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-283\li283{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}{\lang2057 
Add to our political activities and work towards heightening our political influence in the areas that hold the greatest significance
 for our members and for society in general. For example Telecommunication legislation, IT-education and national IT-politics.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-283\li283{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}{\lang2057 Strengthening the co-operation with other similar national organisations.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-283\li283{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}{\lang2057 Strengthening international co-operation and motivate members to participate in international activities.
\par }\pard {\lang2057 
\par }\pard {\lang2057 
\par }\pard\plain \s21\sb120\sa120 \shading10000 \b\f4\fs28\lang1044 {\lang2057 The NCS Working groups
\par }\pard\plain \f4\fs20\lang1044 {\lang2057 \tab NCS has three national working groups: Tele- and Datacommunication, Multimedia and IT and Education. In addition NCS has 22 local working groups within separate fields of expertis
e. All the working groups are tied to the Societies nine local societies, who are responsible for the working groups\rquote 
 finances and their activities. The main board of the Society has as one of its responsibilities to encourage the inception of working groups in central fields of expertise.
\par }\pard {\lang2057 \tab Activities in the working groups range from; membership meetings, projects, in-depth studies, seminars, information distribution, informal meetings, and so on. The goal is that the Society should have 40 working groups i
n action this year, which amounts to a marked increase in member activity in the Society.
\par }\pard {\lang2057 
\par }\pard\plain \s21\sb120\sa120 \shading10000 \b\f4\fs28\lang1044 {\lang2057 Events - including international events (IFIP) - in 1995
\par }\pard\plain \f4\fs20\lang1044 {\lang2057 \tab 
NCS is responsible for organising a large number of different seminars, conferences and exhibitions. There were 102 of these events in 1994. And of course the membership meetings are also the responsibility of NCS, and there were a total of 128 such meet
ings in 1994.
\par }\pard {\lang2057 \tab These are some of the events in 1995:
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-283\li283{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}{\lang2057 SOFTWARE\rquote 95. Exhibition and conference. 18.000 visitors in total, and 1.100 attended the conferences. 

\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}BarIT\rquote 95. The first IT-conference for the Barents region in the northernmost part of Norway. 150 participants.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-283\li283{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}{\lang2057 NordDATA'95. Nordic conference in Bergen. 450 participants.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-283\li283{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}{\lang2057 INTERACT\rquote 
95. International IFIP conference on human-computer interaction, with both tutorials and workshops. 180 participants.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}Hjem&Data'95. The first exhibition and conference directed at the private market for computers and related products and services. 
\par }\pard {\lang2057 
\par }\pard\plain \s21\sb120\sa120 \shading10000 \b\f4\fs28\lang1044 {\lang2057 Product development:\line Special offers to personal members / Company members
\par }\pard\plain \f4\fs20\lang1044 {\lang2057 \tab 
NCS is working to improve and renew the special offers to the members in accordance with the different target groups in the member base. The work has just begun to promote the Society on the World Wide Web (http://www.oslonett.no/DND_home.html), and the 
start up of a BBS (Bulletin Board System) is imminent. The BBS will contain numerous newsgroups and conferences, designed to fit the different interests of the members. The different working groups will all have their 
own newsgroup, and the main board will also have a separate and restricted area at its disposal.
\par }\pard {\lang2057 \tab 
The Society offers its members a very affordable contract with an Internet service provider, and also a quality modem at a reasonable price. The offer has been a success, and other offers are planned. Night-tutorials are offered for those who wish to lea
rn more about Internet, and activities and special offers targeted at kids and youth are in the works.
\par }\pard {\lang2057 \tab Special offers have also been developed for company members, such as the publication \ldblquote Checklist for an IT strategy\rdblquote 
, and opportunity to check the soundness of IT contracts (purchase contracts and software licences) that the companies wish to get a second opinion on. This last offer is done in co-operation with
 specialist lawyers. Also offered to our members are reports from international analytical firms, such as ButlerBloor, at bargain rates.
\par }\pard\plain \s21\sb120\sa120 \shading10000 \b\f4\fs28\lang1044 {\lang2057 NCS Publications
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}}\pard\plain \fi-283\li283{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\f4\fs20\lang1044 {\b\lang2057 DND-Nytt (NCS-News)\line }{\lang2057 
The members magazine. Written and designed in-house at the DND Servicekontoret AS. Published four times a year. Circulation 12.000.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-283\li283{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}{\b\lang2057 DND P\'e5 Siden (NCS On the Page)\line }{\lang2057 
An information/news page once a week in Computerworld Norway, a national computer weekly.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\b\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}}\pard \fi-283\li283{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnstart1\pnindent283\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}{\b\lang2057 Between two and four books are published each year.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\b\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}Documentation from conferences are published: 50 - 100 each year.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\b\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}Reports from working groups
\par }\pard {\lang2057 
\par }\pard\plain \s21\sb120\sa120 \shading10000 \b\f4\fs28\lang1044 {\lang2057 New target groups
\par }\pard\plain \f4\fs20\lang1044 {\lang2057 \tab The Society is about to put together several offers for the private market, and is for the first time arranging the exhibition Hjem&Data'95 (Home&Data\rquote 95). The exhibition is ex
pected to draw children and youth, and a teenager is actually a part of the steering committee. It\rquote s also expected that Hjem&Data'95 will draw those computer beginners who have a certain curiosity for the technology. 
\par }\pard {\lang2057 \tab Children and youth are a new target group for the Society, as are teachers.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s21\sb120\sa120 \shading10000 \b\f4\fs28\lang1044 {\lang2057 Activities towards governmental and political authorities
\par }\pard\plain \f4\fs20\lang1044 {\lang2057 \tab NCS works toward politicians, governmental and public institutions in order to influence the legislation made in relation to telecommunication and national I
T strategies. The Society has a good working relationship with the different sections of the government, and is engaged in the follow-up of policy decisions and legislation. NCS works toward putting IT political matters on the national agenda.
\par }\pard {\lang2057 
